phpr-server for Debian
======================

This is NOT php-fpm
-------------------
php-server speaks plain HTTP and serves a document root itself; it
does not implement the FastCGI protocol, so an nginx/Apache
`fastcgi_pass` configuration will not talk to it and this package
intentionally does not Provide php-fpm. To publish sites behind a real
web server, use a reverse proxy:

    location / { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080; }

Service
-------
phpr-server.service runs /usr/bin/php-server --axum as www-data,
enabled by default on 127.0.0.1:8080 with document root
/var/www/html. All knobs live in /etc/default/phpr-server:

    PHPR_HOST=127.0.0.1
    PHPR_PORT=8080
    PHPR_DOCROOT=/var/www/html
    PHPR_WORKERS=0   # 0 = one worker per CPU

After changing it: systemctl restart phpr-server.

Notes
-----
 * --axum mode does not honour a router.php script (the cli-server
   mode, `php-server` without --axum, does).
 * PHP scripts run per-request on a fresh VM in a fixed worker pool;
   there is no request killer / slowlog / process manager like FPM's
   (pm.max_children), only the fixed --workers count.
 * SIGTERM performs a graceful drain and exit; there is no reload
   signal semantics (restart the unit instead).

Feature requests and gaps: https://github.com/francescotinti/php-rust/issues
